# ===== 114.41 Level III, Intermediate Low to Intermediate Mid =====
H('41.c.1.A',3,"At Level III a student answers a question about a topic beyond daily routines, such as a school trip abroad, and adds details. This is:","going beyond everyday topics with elaboration",["repeating a memorized phrase","answering yes or no only","avoiding the topic"],"Level III extends past everyday life with simple elaboration.")
H('41.c.1.A',3,"Which response goes beyond everyday life with elaboration?","I would like to visit a museum because I enjoy history, and the exhibits change every month.",["Museum.","Yes.","I do not know."],"Elaboration adds reasons and details.")
H('41.c.1.B',3,"Giving a recommendation, such as suggesting a book and explaining why, is part of:","exchanging opinions and recommendations",["reading a map","completing a lab","filling in a form"],"Recommendations include supporting statements.")
H('41.c.1.B',3,"Which statement includes a recommendation with support?","I recommend the park because it is quiet and has shade.",["Park.","I like it.","The park is a place."],"A recommendation includes a reason.")
H('41.c.1.C',3,"A speaker says, You must study tonight because the test counts for a quarter of your grade. The speaker is:","telling what someone must do with a reason",["asking a favor","describing weather","telling a joke"],"Obligation is paired with a reason.")
H('41.c.1.C',3,"In written conversation, how can a student give advice with supporting reasons?","by writing what the friend should do and why",["by listing random facts","by copying a headline","by drawing a map"],"Advice includes reasons.")
H('41.c.1.D',3,"Which sentence offers a suggestion and a supporting statement?","Let's meet earlier so we have time to finish the poster.",["Poster.","Meet.","We finish."],"Suggestions are followed by reasons.")
H('41.c.1.D',3,"Developing a plan in conversation means the speakers:","decide together what to do, when and how",["argue without conclusion","avoid decisions","list unrelated items"],"Plans involve shared decisions.")
H('41.c.1.E',3,"Reacting appropriately in conversation includes:","using register and gestures that fit the culture",["using the same expression for everyone","ignoring the listener","speaking as fast as possible"],"Reactions follow cultural norms.")
H('41.c.1.E',3,"Switching from casual talk with a friend to a more formal tone with a principal shows control of:","register",["alphabet","spelling","punctuation only"],"Register adapts to the listener.")
H('41.c.1.F',3,"A written reply to a friend's message should reflect:","culturally appropriate expressions and style",["only abbreviations","random words","complete silence"],"Writing style fits audience and culture.")
H('41.c.1.F',3,"Which closing suits a formal email to a school director?","With respect, followed by your full name",["See ya","Whatever","Bye bye"],"Formal closings fit formal contexts.")
H('41.c.2.A',3,"Understanding a podcast made for native speakers shows a learner can work with:","authentic audio material",["only teacher-made drills","only textbook charts","only handwriting"],"Authentic material is made for speakers of the language.")
H('41.c.2.A',3,"A learner reads a news website from another country. This is:","authentic digital material",["a worksheet","a coloring page","a fill-in-the-blank quiz"],"Digital content from speakers is authentic.")
H('41.c.2.B',3,"To paraphrase the main idea of a short film, a learner should:","restate the idea in different words",["copy the subtitles","list actors only","skip to the credits"],"Paraphrasing shows understanding.")
H('41.c.2.B',3,"Which is a supporting detail in a story about a market day?","what vendors sold and how the crowd reacted",["the title of the document","the font size","the date of printing"],"Details support the main idea.")
H('41.c.2.C',3,"A learner meets a new word in a contextualized video. The best approach is to:","use surrounding images and words to infer meaning",["stop immediately","ignore the video","guess randomly"],"Inference uses context.")
H('41.c.2.C',3,"Which clue helps infer meaning of an unfamiliar phrase in a conversation?","the speaker's tone and the situation",["the page number","the weather report","the font"],"Tone and situation give clues.")
H('41.c.2.D',3,"Comparing how families celebrate a holiday in two cultures is:","contrasting cultural practices",["comparing math results","contrasting spelling rules","measuring distances"],"Practices are compared across cultures.")
H('41.c.2.D',3,"After watching two videos of school life in different countries, a learner notes both similarities and differences. This is:","comparing and contrasting cultural practices",["copying vocabulary","ignoring details","avoiding the topic"],"Comparison involves likeness and difference.")
H('41.c.3.A',3,"Defending an opinion in a speech means:","giving reasons and examples to support it",["repeating it quietly","changing it constantly","avoiding any reasons"],"Defending adds support.")
H('41.c.3.A',3,"Which written opinion includes support and elaboration?","I believe students need more sleep because tired students learn less, and many schools start too early.",["Sleep.","Students.","I believe."],"Elaboration strengthens opinions.")
H('41.c.3.B',3,"Narrating an event with connected sentences, details and elaboration means telling it:","in order with specific information",["as a list of words","in a single sentence","with no details"],"Narration needs sequence and detail.")
H('41.c.3.B',3,"Which sentence helps narrate an event with detail?","Last Saturday, we hiked a trail near the river and saw three deer.",["Hike.","River.","Deer."],"Specific details enrich narration.")
H('41.c.3.C',3,"Informing others about a topic in writing at Level III includes:","connected sentences with details",["one-word answers","a single phrase","only a title"],"Informative writing connects sentences and details.")
H('41.c.3.C',3,"Which task is an example of informing others orally?","giving a short talk on how a local festival began",["copying a recipe","silently reading","drawing a map"],"Informing explains facts to an audience.")

# ===== 114.42 Level IV, Intermediate Mid to Intermediate High =====
H('42.c.1.A',4,"At Level IV a student answers a question about an event outside daily routine with elaboration. This shows:","elaboration beyond everyday topics",["single-word answers","avoidance","memorized scripts only"],"Level IV elaborates on varied topics.")
H('42.c.1.A',4,"Which response shows elaboration at Level IV?","I think public transportation helps cities because it reduces traffic and pollution.",["Yes.","Maybe.","It is."],"Elaboration includes reasons.")
H('42.c.1.B',4,"Responding to a question in an unfamiliar context with limited vocabulary requires the student to:","use circumlocution and clarifying strategies",["stop speaking","switch to another subject","ignore the question"],"Strategies help in unfamiliar situations.")
H('42.c.1.B',4,"A student does not know a word and describes it with other words instead. This strategy is:","circumlocution",["copying","silence","spelling"],"Circumlocution means talking around a word.")
H('42.c.1.C',4,"Exchanging opinions and recommendations at Level IV includes:","supporting elaborative statements",["one-word replies","unrelated jokes","copied sentences"],"Elaborative support deepens exchange.")
H('42.c.1.C',4,"Which pair shows an opinion with elaborative support?","I prefer the first plan. It is cheaper, and it needs less time.",["Plan.","I do not know.","Yes. Plan."],"Support follows the opinion.")
H('42.c.1.D',4,"Telling someone what they must do using detailed rationale means:","explaining the reasons behind the instruction",["giving only commands","avoiding reasons","using one word"],"Rationale explains why.")
H('42.c.1.D',4,"Which statement gives a detailed rationale?","You should wear a helmet since it protects your head and many local rules require it.",["Wear it.","Helmet.","Do it."],"Rationale supports the advice.")
H('42.c.1.E',4,"Articulating requests, offering suggestions and developing plans with elaborative statements shows:","extended planning conversation",["a single request","silence","scripted lines"],"Plans involve extended talk.")
H('42.c.1.E',4,"A student proposes, Let's hold the fundraiser in spring since the weather is better and more families can attend. This is:","a suggestion with elaboration",["a refusal","a question only","a greeting"],"The suggestion has reasons.")
H('42.c.1.F',4,"Interacting and reacting in spoken conversation with culturally appropriate gestures shows:","sociolinguistic awareness",["only memorized scripts","only reading skill","only writing skill"],"Appropriate gestures show cultural awareness.")
H('42.c.1.F',4,"A student shifts register when speaking with an elder versus a peer. This demonstrates:","cultural appropriateness",["confusion","guessing","avoidance"],"Register choice respects culture.")
H('42.c.1.G',4,"In a written exchange with a pen pal, a student's response should:","address the pen pal's points in an appropriate style",["ignore the content","copy the pen pal's message","use only symbols"],"Interactive writing responds to the other person.")
H('42.c.1.G',4,"Which element reflects culturally appropriate written style in an email to an official?","a formal greeting and closing",["emojis only","no greeting","slang"],"Formal contexts need formal style.")
H('42.c.2.A',4,"Analyzing a culturally authentic documentary requires a learner to:","look at content, perspective and cultural context",["watch with the sound off","skip the middle","memorize the title"],"Analysis considers context.")
H('42.c.2.A',4,"Which material would a Level IV student analyze in a variety of contexts?","an article or video made for speakers of the language",["a teacher-made worksheet","a blank grid","a spelling list"],"Authentic materials are the basis of analysis.")
H('42.c.2.B',4,"To paraphrase and analyze a text's theme, a learner:","restates the central idea and explains how details support it",["copies the title","lists unrelated facts","skips details"],"Analysis connects theme and details.")
H('42.c.2.B',4,"Which is an analysis of supporting details?","explaining how examples in a story develop its message",["counting pages","naming the author","copying a quote"],"Analysis explains how details work.")
H('42.c.2.C',4,"Inferring meaning of unfamiliar words in a text relies on:","context, word parts and prior knowledge",["random guessing","ignoring clues","the font"],"Inference uses multiple clues.")
H('42.c.2.C',4,"A learner knows a prefix and root in a new word. Using them to guess the meaning is:","an inference strategy",["a copying task","a spelling error","a pronunciation exercise"],"Word parts help inference.")
H('42.c.2.D',4,"Comparing perspectives on a historic event from two authentic sources is:","contrasting cultural practices and perspectives",["measuring angles","naming rivers","copying captions"],"Perspective comparison is a Level IV skill.")
H('42.c.2.D',4,"Why do perspectives from two cultures about the same holiday sometimes differ?","because history and values shape how a group sees an event",["because holidays are random","because languages are identical","because there are no values"],"Perspectives reflect culture.")
H('42.c.3.A',4,"Persuading others in a speech involves:","claims, support and elaborative statements",["silence","one-word answers","unrelated stories"],"Persuasion uses claims and support.")
H('42.c.3.A',4,"Which opening is most persuasive?","Our school needs a garden because it teaches science and builds community.",["Garden.","We have gardens.","Gardens are green."],"Persuasion states a claim with reasons.")
H('42.c.3.B',4,"Narrating with some connected discourse means the narrator:","links sentences with transitions and details",["lists events with no links","uses only one word","speaks in fragments"],"Connected discourse flows.")
H('42.c.3.B',4,"Which phrase signals a transition in a narrative?","after that, later on",["blue sky","the number five","a red shoe"],"Transitions connect events.")
H('42.c.3.C',4,"Informing others about a topic with some connected discourse requires:","organized paragraphs with transitions",["bullet fragments only","one phrase","a title only"],"Organization supports information.")
H('42.c.3.C',4,"Which is a strong way to inform an audience about recycling?","give facts, examples and clear connections between them",["recite a single word","draw without text","avoid explaining"],"Information needs clear connections.")

# ===== 114.43 Level V, Intermediate High to Advanced Mid =====
H('43.c.1.A',4,"Using generally consistent register in all time frames means a speaker:","keeps an appropriate tone while talking about past, present and future",["only speaks about the present","changes tone randomly","avoids time references"],"Register stays consistent across time frames.")
H('43.c.1.A',4,"Which skill separates Level V conversation from earlier levels?","sustaining discussion across past, present and future",["using only memorized lines","answering yes or no","avoiding abstract topics"],"Level V handles all time frames.")
H('43.c.1.B',4,"Verbally exchanging information on a variety of geographic, cultural and academic topics requires:","broad vocabulary and appropriate register",["only greetings","only numbers","only names"],"Broad topics require broad language.")
H('43.c.1.B',4,"A student discusses climate in one region and economic trends in another. This shows:","ability to exchange information on varied topics",["a single-topic script","silence","random chatter"],"Variety of topics is a Level V goal.")
H('43.c.1.C',4,"Writing a business-style letter that keeps a formal register across time frames shows:","consistent register in writing",["inconsistent tone","only informal slang","copied phrases"],"Written register is consistent.")
H('43.c.1.C',4,"Which written item might a Level V student produce with consistent register?","a formal letter of inquiry",["a list of single words","a drawing","a grocery list only"],"Correspondence uses consistent register.")
H('43.c.1.D',4,"A written exchange that provides information on a topic of interest reflects:","clear, organized, detailed writing",["fragmented notes","unrelated sentences","silent reading"],"Written exchanges present information.")
H('43.c.1.D',4,"Which written response keeps register consistent with a formal reader?","a polished message with appropriate vocabulary and closing",["a casual text with slang","a single emoji","a note without greeting"],"Register must fit the reader.")
H('43.c.2.A',4,"Reading and analyzing artwork or a news article from the target culture requires:","attention to content, context and perspective",["only skimming the title","ignoring images","reading the last line only"],"Analysis uses multiple layers.")
H('43.c.2.A',4,"Which resource might a Level V learner analyze?","a magazine, an artwork description or a government website in the target language",["a blank page","a teacher quiz","an alphabet chart"],"Authentic resources are the basis of analysis.")
H('43.c.2.B',4,"Comparing cultural perspectives from authentic print sources means:","examining how viewpoints differ and why",["copying passages","skipping context","listing page numbers"],"Perspective comparison is analytic.")
H('43.c.2.B',4,"Why analyze cultural practices alongside perspectives?","practices reflect the values behind them",["practices are unrelated to values","perspectives do not matter","analysis is optional"],"Practices and perspectives are linked.")
H('43.c.2.C',4,"Listening to an interview made for native speakers and explaining its main points shows:","analysis of authentic audio",["note copying","ignoring the audio","reading only"],"Audio analysis requires comprehension.")
H('43.c.2.C',4,"Which strategy helps analyze a rapid audio recording?","listening for tone, key terms and structure",["turning off the sound","ignoring the speaker","only counting words"],"Analysis uses multiple cues.")
H('43.c.2.D',4,"Analyzing cultural perspectives in an audiovisual documentary means identifying:","the viewpoint of the creators and the audience",["only the length","only the credits","the file format"],"Perspective analysis considers creators.")
H('43.c.2.D',4,"Comparing a documentary from one culture with a film from another reveals:","differences in values, practices and storytelling",["identical content","no difference","nothing at all"],"Comparison highlights difference.")
H('43.c.3.A',4,"Planning, producing and presenting a spoken presentation with some ease and clarity means:","organizing ideas and delivering them clearly",["reading unrelated notes","speaking without plan","avoiding the audience"],"Planning and delivery matter.")
H('43.c.3.A',4,"A Level V presenter prepares an outline, practices and speaks to an audience. This is:","presentational communication",["silent reading","random speaking","copying text"],"Presentations are planned for an audience.")
H('43.c.3.B',4,"Planning and producing a written presentation such as an article with clear expression requires:","drafting, revising and organizing ideas",["one-word answers","copying others","skipping planning"],"Written work is drafted and revised.")
H('43.c.3.B',4,"Which stage improves the clarity of a written presentation?","revising and editing for organization and word choice",["ignoring errors","deleting content","adding unrelated text"],"Revision improves clarity.")
